  "output": {
    "svg": "architecture.svg",
    "medium": "documentation and notebook",
    "alt_text": "A root request reaches an untrusted supervisor that may only propose a dispatch. A trusted control plane validates the workload edge and reserves from one shared depth, fan-out, dispatch, and affected-component budget. One retry owner admits only transient retries and combines per-component circuits with queue bulkheads. Research, billing, and ticket or messaging workers are isolated fault domains with no worker-to-worker edges. A poison signal activates a containment switch that clears queues and blocks effects. Only a successful bound attempt can reach the atomic idempotent effect gate, and all decisions emit content-free receipts."
  },
